00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:05.200 align:start position:0%
eu ministers for education meeting on  friday  will discuss the development of  entrepreneurial skills through education  and training  they will adopt conclusions highlighting  the importance of promoting  entrepreneurship  from an early age and of reinforcing  links between the education system  and the business world the conclusions  invite member states to fully exploit  the potential  that the erasmus plus program offers in  supporting entrepreneurship education  as well as to make the best use of the  other european resources  such as the european social fund the  contribution of the education sector to  growth and jobs  is also on the agenda a public debate  will be held to analyze the role of  education  in view of the midterm review of the eu  2020 strategy  in the afternoon the discussions will  focus on youth issues  the council will adopt conclusion on  young people's access to rights in order  to foster their autonomy and  participation in society  the effects of the economic crisis have  diminished young people's capacity for  autonomy  ministers will highlight the need to  develop strategies and policies  that guarantee access to services and  education supporting young people's  progress  towards self-sufficiency and citizenship  finally a discussion will be held on how  a cross-sectoral approach to youth  policies  can work as a tool for better tackling  socio-economic challenges  today in the eu 21.6 of young people  between 15 and 24  are unemployed the idea is to discuss  how cooperation between different policy  sectors  can reduce youth unemployment  you
 

